 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax in\nthe town of Cortlandt",
    "basePrintNo": "S7887",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7887-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-nnn, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7887\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax\nin the town of Cortlandt\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Town of Cortlandt, Westchester County, to levy a hotel\noccupancy tax not to exceed three percent.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section 1202-nnn to the Tax Law, which will author-\nize and empower the Town of Cortlandt, Westchester County, to adopt and\namend local laws imposing a tax on rented hotel rooms, which is not to\nexceed 3%. It also defines the term hotel as a building or a portion of\na building that is regularly used for the lodging of guests, and\nincludes apartment hotels, motels, or boarding houses.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAt the request of the Supervisor and Board, the Town of Cortlandt wishes\nto join the likes of other Westchester County towns (Greenburgh, Mount\nPleasant and North Castle) in enacting a hotel occupancy tax.\n\nAs many individuals and municipalities face financial hardships, some\nintensified by the COVID-19 pandemic, it is imperative that property tax\nincreases be kept minimal while still allowing towns to provide neces-\nsary services.\n\nThe timing of this request is optimal as a new hotel is proposed to be\nbuilt on Route 6 (Cortlandt Boulevard) near the Bear Mountain Parkway,\nand once enacted, this legislation will provide the Town of Cortlandt\nwith an additional source of revenue.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNA.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
